course: dictionary
lesson: 10996
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «Wash your hands with soap for 20 seconds» means clean them with water and soap, because that is what you do to hands.
explain: «The boat washed ashore.» Here wash means carried by water. The sea moved the boat onto the beach. Check by swapping in carried: «The boat was carried ashore» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Wash can also be a noun, meaning an act of washing: «Give the car a wash.» In «Dyes wash out» it means something is removed by water, and in «the clothes are in the wash» it means clothes that are being washed.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Wash is a verb: wash, washes, washed, washing. It can also be a noun: a wash.
fact: Wash can mean to clean with water and usually soap, or to be carried by water.
fact: «Washing» can also mean the clothes that are being washed, as in «in the wash».
fact: Phrases with wash include wash up, wash away, washing machine and car wash.
exercise: «Wash your hands with soap for 20 seconds before eating.» What does wash mean here? | *To clean with water and soap | Clothes that are being washed | A machine that dries clothes | To be carried by water
exercise: «The boat washed ashore.» What does washed mean here? | Was cleaned with soap | Was painted white | Was sunk in the sea | *Was carried by water onto the land
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Give the car a wash.» that is a noun. | *wash | car | the | Give
test: «Dyes can also leave: they wash out, rub off and fade in sunlight.» What does wash out mean here? | Are added to the cloth | Are made brighter by sunlight | Are sold in shops | *Are removed by water
test: «Farmers cut steps called terraces so the flat steps hold water and stop soil washing away.» What does washing away mean here? | Being cleaned with soap | Being used to grow rice | *Being carried off by water | Being dug up by hand
exam: «A girl in Sydney reaches into the washing-up for a spoon and finds a sharp knife.» What does washing-up mean? | Clothes in the washing machine | *Dirty dishes that are being washed | A cloth used to dry the floor | Water that is dirty
